## Section-Type Guidance

{% if section_type == 'hero' %}
### Hero Section Best Practices
- Create strong visual impact with a full-width or near-full-width layout
- Place a clear, compelling CTA above the fold with a high-contrast button
- Lead with a concise value proposition in the H1 headline
- Add a supporting subheadline that expands on the benefit
- Use a hero image or gradient background that reinforces the brand
- Include social proof near the CTA (e.g., "Trusted by 10,000+ teams")
- Ensure the entire hero is visible without scrolling on common viewports
{% elif section_type == 'features' %}
### Features Section Best Practices
- Use a scannable grid or card layout (2-3 columns on desktop, stacked on mobile)
- Include an icon or illustration for each feature to aid visual scanning
- Write clear, benefit-oriented headings for each feature
- Keep feature descriptions concise (1-2 sentences)
- Maintain consistent card sizing and spacing
- Consider a "Learn more" link per feature for deeper exploration
{% elif section_type == 'pricing' %}
### Pricing Section Best Practices
- Use a comparison table or side-by-side card layout for plans
- Visually highlight the recommended or most popular plan with a border, badge, or scale difference
- Make CTAs prominent and distinct for each plan ("Start Free", "Go Pro", "Contact Sales")
- List features with checkmarks or icons for easy scanning
- Show monthly/annual toggle if both billing options exist
- Keep the pricing clear and unambiguous -- no hidden fees
{% elif section_type == 'testimonials' %}
### Testimonials Section Best Practices
- Display social proof prominently: real names, titles, company names
- Include author photos (or placeholder avatars) to add credibility
- Use star ratings or numeric scores where available
- Style quotation marks or pull-quote formatting for visual distinction
- Show 2-3 testimonials at a time; use a carousel or grid for more
- Add company logos if the testimonials come from notable brands
{% elif section_type == 'cta' %}
### CTA Section Best Practices
- Add urgency elements where authentic (e.g., "Limited time", "Join 5,000+ users")
- Use a contrasting button color that pops against the section background
- Write a clear benefit statement as the heading (e.g., "Start saving 10 hours a week")
- Keep the section focused -- one primary action, minimal distractions
- Add a secondary supporting line below the heading for reassurance
- Surround the CTA with generous whitespace to draw the eye
{% elif section_type == 'faq' %}
### FAQ Section Best Practices
- Use an accordion-style layout so users can expand/collapse answers
- Group questions into clear categories if there are many
- Write questions in the user's voice (e.g., "How do I cancel?" not "Cancellation Policy")
- Keep answers concise and scannable; use bullet points where appropriate
- Consider a search bar or filter for large FAQ sets
- Link to related support articles or contact options at the bottom
{% else %}
### General Section Best Practices
- Ensure clear visual hierarchy with a section heading and supporting content
- Use consistent spacing and alignment with the rest of the page
- Make the section responsive across all breakpoints
{% endif %}

